maria: Heads-up: docs PR #4872 — updating SDK examples for streaming cancellation + resume. Need tiny TS, Py, Go samples. Also fix broken link in streams.md. Who can pick up code snippets?
ajay: :wave: I can do TS + tests. Can you outline desired behavior? cancel semantics vs. graceful close?
maria: Thanks! Need three things: 1) show how to cancel streaming response client-side (AbortController/ctx), 2) show resuming a stream using continuation cursor when partial tokens received, 3) show safe retry/backoff for idempotent streams. Keep examples minimal.
liam: I'll handle Python + docs text. For resume, prefer an example using 'resume_token' header returned by server. Let's standardize header name: X-Redwood-Resume-Token.
sophia: Go snippet for context cancellation + receiving chunks over channel. Also include example of checking 'X-Redwood-Resume-Token' in response headers to resume.
ajay: Draft TS snippet pushed to my branch ajay/streams-snippets. Quick preview here:
```ts
const controller = new AbortController();
const res = await fetch('/v1/generate/stream', {signal: controller.signal});
for await (const chunk of streamChunks(res.body)) {
  console.log(chunk.text);
  if (chunk.partial && chunk.cursor) {
    // save cursor to DB
    saveCursor(chunk.cursor);
  }
}
// cancel example
controller.abort();
```
Is that too hand-wavy?
maria: Nice. Add a tiny helper: streamChunks = async function*(body) { /* async iterator for ReadableStream */ } so readers know pattern. And show using AbortController to stop.
liam: Python draft:
```py
